BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film screening of Parade: Queer Acts of Love and Resistance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T190000
UID:69e7ff951e64afd01e6ad0e2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a film screening from the National Film Board.\nPa
 rade: Queer Acts of Love & Resistance\ncaptures pivotal moments that spark
 ed Canada’s 2SLGBTQI+ movement\, honouring the activists and elders whos
 e resistance led to the rights we have today.\nThrough rarely seen archiva
 l footage and first-person accounts\, audiences are brought to the frontli
 nes of the struggle. From police raids to early drag shows\, community org
 anizing to the House of Commons—the complex history of the country’s d
 iverse communities is brought to life. Key milestones illustrate the power
  of taking it into the streets and underscore how easily the rights we’v
 e fought for can be revoked\, making the documentary essential viewing for
  all Canadians.\nUnflinching\, bold\, enraging\, hopeful\;\nParade\nis a v
 ital new chapter in the queer canon.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Room B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e7ff951e64afd01e6ad0e2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Craft and Chat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T190000
UID:69a0928f4a9fd98b7f80bfe8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Feeling crafty?\nDo you like to crochet\, embroider\, knit\, j
 ournal\, or something else entirely? If you are looking to chat with some 
 fellow crafters while enjoying your favourite hobby\, come join our Craft 
 and Chat.\nCraft and socialize in a friendly and welcoming environment. Un
 leash your talent\, express your creativity\, and make new friends.\nJoin 
 us weekly for a fun hour of creativity. All skill levels welcome.\nA limit
 ed supply of materials will be available\, so please bring your own suppli
 es and a small project\, if you have them.\nLimited instruction available 
 for beginners in cross-stitch.\nDrop in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Centre of room at Canoe Table
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a0928f4a9fd98b7f80bfe8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monday Night at the Movies!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T200000
UID:6a16220e2ea730c17ab1e907@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come enjoy a night at the Port Union Cinema!\nWe will be showi
 ng the following movie at this event:\nThunderBolts\nAfter finding themsel
 ves ensnared in a death trap set by Valentina Allegra de Fontaine\, these 
 disillusioned castoffs must embark on a dangerous mission that will force 
 them to confront the darkest corners of their pasts. Will this dysfunction
 al group tear themselves apart\, or find redemption and unite as something
  much more before it's too late?\nThis is a BYoP event. (Bring Your Own Po
 pcorn.)**
LOCATION:Port Union\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a16220e2ea730c17ab1e907
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
