BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Sharon Alex
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T235959
UID:6a20399b748daf857d5ab32a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, the works of artist Sharon Alex
  are on display at Albion Branch\nSharon is an artist based in Toronto. S
 he paints in watercolours and loves photography. Her poetry explores her i
 nner most thoughts and hope she opens something within yourself as well\n
 "I'm inspired by animals and nature and poetry. My purpose is to tap into 
 the intimate and make you pause and explore what is important to you".\nTh
 is exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Li
 brary provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations 
 across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural intere
 sts of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during 
 Albion branch's open hours. Please check the\nAlbion branch\npage before y
 ou visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nPhoto credit: Sharon Alex\,\nThe Monar
 ch\, Photograph\, 8x10.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a20399b748daf857d5ab32a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Sinye Tang
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T235959
UID:6a299f022ea730c17ab5e08e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, works by artist Sinye Tang are 
 on display at Don Mills Branch.\nSinye Tang (she/her) is a Chinese-Canadia
 n artist\, food enthusiast\, and amateur kayaker residing in Toronto. Her 
 artwork is informed by urban forays into nature and in search of deliciou
 s bites. She enjoys starting her watercolours in nature or on the water\, 
 and collaborates often with her husband\, Evan Manuella\, on line and was
 h.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Pu
 blic Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at loc
 ations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural
  interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed 
 during branch open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a299f022ea730c17ab5e08e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Queer & Trans Sex-Ed You Should Have Gotten in High School
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T150000
UID:69fe035b17731928001856de@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Queer & trans adults deserve a space that centers their needs 
 to learn how to have healthy relationships and sexual experiences. In this
  shame-free\, fun\, and interactive workshop presented by Eva Bloom\, an a
 ward-winning educator and speaker\, attendees will learn communication fra
 meworks\, queer & trans inclusive pleasure anatomy\, sex & dating beyond C
 IS heteronormative scripts\, and how to manage their sexual health.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe035b17731928001856de
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google AI Essentials: In Person Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T150000
UID:69fe4de51773192800186f03@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about artificial intelligence or want to learn practic
 al AI skills for work and personal use? Join our staff-facilitated learnin
 g circle to complete the self-paced Google AI Essentials specialization.\n
 This 10-hour introductory-level specialization\, offered through Coursera\
 , is available for free to learning circle participants. It is made up of 
 five courses\, each containing four units that consist of short videos\, a
 rticles\, assignments and a short multiple-choice quiz.\nBy completing the
  specialization\,\nyou will learn:\nHow AI works\nHow to write effective p
 rompts\nHow to use generative AI tools responsibly\nHow to identify AI's p
 otential biases and avoid harm\nHow to stay up to date with AI news\nAfter
  you complete the course\, you earn a Google certificate and a badge to sh
 are with others\nLearning Circles are study groups guided by\nlibrary staf
 f for people who want to complete the Google AI Essentials specialization 
 together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work together thr
 ough course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit to attending a
 ll four learning circle sessions.\nNo AI experience is required.\nHow to J
 oin\na Learning Circle:\nRegister once on the first session of this event 
 series\, in order to attend all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a\nvalid em
 ail address\n.\nA valid TPL library card is required for online circles.
 \nAttend all four sessions (in person at\nbranch name\n)\nRegistration is 
 a two-step procedure. First\, participants must complete their registratio
 n through this page. After this step\, library staff will follow up to req
 uest additional information in order to complete the registration.\nInform
 ation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collect
 ed by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections
  20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event an
 d program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the 
 library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\na
 nswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe4de51773192800186f03
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
