BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Generate Music with Gesture
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T180000
UID:69a203be1e64afd01e5e90f0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could create music just by waving your hands\, mov
 ing your body\, or holding up an object? In this workshop\, you'll discove
 r how AI and motion-sensing technology can turn real-world movements into 
 ever-changing soundscapes.\nYou'll use AI to generate original ambient sou
 nd materials\, then connect them to a visual program that responds to your
  gestures\, movements\, and even objects in the room - turning your body i
 nto a musical instrument. No prior music or programming experience is requ
 ired.\nRegistration is required.\nThis program is part of the Innovator in
  Residence (AI and Music Production) program\, which is designed to help b
 eginner and intermediate learners build knowledge and creative skills and 
 get hands-on with current AI tools in music production and learn about the
  history\, copyright and ethics of generative music. For more information 
 and a full list of programs\, visit tpl.ca/airesident.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Digital Innovation Hub\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a203be1e64afd01e5e90f0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
