BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Contraception Conversation: Choices\, Myths & Real Talk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T190000
UID:6a0f50bd8ea300e263178ffe@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Understanding your reproductive health is an important part of
  overall wellbeing\, but with so much information — and misinformation 
 — online\, it can be difficult to know what’s accurate or which contra
 ception option may be right for you.\nWhether you are considering contrace
 ption for the first time\, looking to change methods\, or simply wanting t
 o learn more\, this session will offer practical knowledge and guidance to
  support informed\, confident choices.\nWhat to Expect:\nYour Cycle\n: Lea
 rn about the menstrual cycle and anatomy of the reproductive organs.\nCont
 raception Options:\nLearn the history of contraception and the hormonal an
 d non-hormonal options we have available today.\nMyths and Facts:\nLearn a
 bout common social media myths about contraception.\nYour Body\, Your Choi
 ce:\nWhat questions to ask and how to pick the best option for you.\nAshle
 y Dixon and Niru Bhanderi are Nurse Practitioners (NPs) at the Bay Centre 
 at Women’s College Hospital providing comprehensive and inclusive sexual
  healthcare services to all genders. Ashley is a Menopause Society Certifi
 ed Practitioner and also works at the NP-Led Menopause clinic at Women’s
  College. She is interested in how sex and gender influence health and enj
 oys helping people feel informed\, confident\, and empowered to make choic
 es that align with their goals and values.\nNiru is currently involved in 
 a research study that is investigating inhaled analgesics for IUD insertio
 n procedures. She is also leading a quality improvement (QI) initiative al
 igning with Choosing Wisely principles in reducing unnecessary preoperativ
 e testing for surgical abortion patients.\nAbout the Series\nBridging Mind
 s: Health & Science Conversations is a partnership between the Toronto Pub
 lic Library and Women’s College Hospital. Through monthly discussions le
 d by experts from across different clinical areas and scientific disciplin
 es\, this series provides attendees with the opportunity to engage directl
 y with our topics and speakers and empowers communities to navigate health
  and science topics confidently\, inspiring a future of informed decision-
 making.\nLearn more:\nhttps://www.womenscollegehospital.ca/bridging-minds/
 \nReserve Your Spot Today!\nThis virtual event is free to join but registr
 ation is required.\nPlease register on Eventbrite\n.\nOnce registered\, yo
 u’ll receive an email with details on how to join the session.\nWe can
 ’t wait to see you there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0f50bd8ea300e263178ffe
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
