BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fashion for the Planet: Clothing & Caretaking
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T200000
UID:6a04a1790c0f2c4503f9fdf4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:With the rise of fast fashion brands and social media fueled c
 onsumption habits\, the fashion industry ranks as the 3rd most environment
 ally damaging industry. Everyone participates in this in some way\, so it 
 is important that people are given the information and tools to consume cl
 othing responsibly. This 4 session program will work towards providing sus
 tainable fashion literacy to participants by teaching them the environment
 al impacts of the fashion industry\, tips for conscious consumption\, and 
 practical tools to extend the life cycle of their clothing through proper 
 care techniques\, mending and alteration skills\, and creative up-cycling 
 workshops.\nThis Session\n: Clothing & Caretaking\nMini hand sewing tutori
 als\nCreative brainstorming for participant’s up-cycling piece\nJune 24t
 h: Collaborative Mending & Upcycling\nParticipants will bring a piece of c
 lothing that needs mending or upcycling & we will work on them by hand tog
 ether\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a04a1790c0f2c4503f9fdf4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
