 ld
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T200000
UID:69dfc8391e64afd01e6962be@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Navigate today’s fast‑paced digital world with clarity and
  confidence. In an era of constant pings\, pop‑ups\, and pressure to sta
 y connected\, our attention is pulled in every direction—yet most advice
  focuses on screen‑time guilt rather than building real inner skills.\nT
 his interactive session offers a fresh approach grounded in the Stoic disc
 iplines of Perception\, Action\, and Will. Through practical strategies\, 
 you’ll explore how to notice digital pulls clearly\, respond with intent
 ion\, and stay aligned with your values amid everyday digital noise.\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dfc8391e64afd01e6962be
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
