BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Outspoken: A Journey from Olympic Athlete to Activist with Author 
 Betty Baxter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T150000
UID:69f12f078ddc1caf5f1fd89a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:When\nBetty Baxter\nwas hired to coach the Canadian women’s 
 volleyball team in 1980\, she faced a media frenzy as the first woman to h
 old the position. In her inspiring debut personal memoir\,\nOutspoken\n: 
 A Journey from Olympic Athlete to Activist\,\nBaxter shares her journey fr
 om small-town prairie girl discovering her passion for sports through year
 s of international success\, including harsh coaches\, excruciating traini
 ng regimes and the inequities in the sports system\, especially for a clos
 eted gay athlete.\nJoin Betty Baxter in conversation with\nMary Ormsby\n\,
  a Canadian journalist and sports editor for the Toronto Star\, as they di
 scuss activism\, the pursuit of gender equality and support for the LGBTQ+
  community\, and the power of being outspoken.\nPresented as part of TPL's
 \nPride Celebration\nprograms.\nRegistration:\nThis virtual event is free 
 to join and will take place on\nZoom\n. Register to receive an email with
  details on how to join the session.\nThis program will not be recorded.\n
 Captions will be available.\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and particip
 ating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nPlace a hold or borrow
  from Toronto Public Library:\nOutspoken\n(book)\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f12f078ddc1caf5f1fd89a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
