BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sharing Your Sound: Build an Online Presence with AI-Generated Mus
 ic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T200000
UID:69a204161e64afd01e5e90fc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You've made something you're proud of. Now what? Whether you w
 ant to share your music with friends\, build a following\, or just get you
 r creations out into the world\, knowing how to present yourself online is
  just as important as making the music itself.\nIn this session\, you'll l
 earn how to take the music you've created and share it with the world. We'
 ll cover the basics of setting up a music profile\, choosing the right pla
 tforms\, creating content that stands out\, and understanding what you can
  and can't do with AI-generated music when posting publicly.\nDrop-in\, no
  registration required.\nThis program is part of the Innovator in Residenc
 e (AI and Music Production) program\, which is designed to help beginner a
 nd intermediate learners build knowledge and creative skills and get hands
 -on with current AI tools in music production and learn about the history\
 , copyright and ethics of generative music. For more information and a ful
 l list of programs\, visit tpl.ca/airesident.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a204161e64afd01e5e90fc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Butterflies On The Brink: The Story of the Mottled Duskywing Scree
 ning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T200000
UID:69e28787b1165a41a65fe3da@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Mottled Duskywing butterfly\, found only in a handful of h
 abitats in Ontario\, is vanishing at an alarming rate. Witness the inspiri
 ng efforts of a dedicated recovery team as they work tirelessly to bring t
 his species back to its former range.\nJoin us for a screening of\nButterf
 lies on the Brink\n: The Story of the Mottled Duskywing\n\, a gripping doc
 umentary about a rare butterfly species' fight for survival on the edge of
  extinction.\nThe film is approximately 47 minutes\, followed by a Q&A pan
 el with\nMiles Finlayson\n\, the director of Butterflies On The Brink\, wi
 th special guests:\nAdrienne Brewster\n\, Executive Director of Cambridge
  Butterfly Conservatory.\nJessica Linton\,\nSenior Biologist and Species a
 t Risk Manager at Natural Resource Solutions Inc. and the Chair of the On
 tario Butterfly Species at Risk Recovery Team.\nDr. Ryan Norris\n\, profes
 sor at the University of Guelph's Department of Integrative Biology\n[Un
 fortunately\, Ryan is no longer available.]\nPresented by the\nDavid Suzuk
 i Foundation\n\, a Canadian environmental non-profit organization with a m
 ission to protect nature’s diversity and the wellbeing of all life\, now
  and for the future.\nFree. Registration required. Doors open at 6:15 pm. 
 At 6:30 pm\, seating becomes first-come\, first-served until capacity is r
 eached.\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series
 \, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​\nQue
 stions? Please contact North York Central Library - Business\, Science & T
 echnology Department.\nThis program is also offered on\nTuesday\, June 2\,
  2026\, 6:30 pm – 8:00 pm\nat\nNorth York Central Library\n.\nYou can a
 lso find more\nDSF programs at TPL\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
 ary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). T
 he information will only be used for event and program registration\, deli
 very and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informat
 ion can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-598
 1\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Theatre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e28787b1165a41a65fe3da
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google AI Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T200000
UID:69fb97a3e7108c0f03d128e3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about artificial intelligence or want to learn practic
 al AI skills for work and personal use? Join our staff-facilitated learnin
 g circle to complete the self-paced Google AI Essentials specialization.\n
 This 10-hour introductory-level specialization\, offered through Coursera\
 , is available for free to learning circle participants. It is made up of 
 five courses\, each containing four units that consist of short videos\, a
 rticles\, assignments and a short multiple-choice quiz.\nBy completing the
  specialization\,\nyou will learn:\nHow AI works\nHow to write effective p
 rompts\nHow to use generative AI tools responsibly\nHow to identify AI's p
 otential biases and avoid harm\nHow to stay up to date with AI news\nAfter
  you complete the course\, you earn a Google certificate and a badge to sh
 are with others\nLearning Circles are study groups guided by\nlibrary staf
 f for people who want to complete the Google AI Essentials specialization 
 together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work together thr
 ough course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit to attending a
 ll four learning circle sessions.\nNo AI experience is required.\nHow to J
 oi\nn a Learning Circle:\nRegister once on the first session of this event
  series\, in order to attend all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a\nvalid e
 mail address\n.\nA valid TPL library card is required for online circles
 .\nAttend all four sessions (online via Zoom\, date: June 4-June 25\, 2026
 )\nRegistration is a two-step procedure. First\, participants must complet
 e their registration through this page. After this step\, library staff wi
 ll follow up to request additional information in order to complete the re
 gistration.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fb97a3e7108c0f03d128e3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
