BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google Prompting Essentials: In Person Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T160000
UID:69fb959c4134893003f0e7ce@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ready to develop the skills to use generative AI (GenAI) tools
  effectively and responsibly for work and daily life? Join our staff-facil
 itated learning circle to complete the self-paced Google Prompting Essenti
 als course. By completing this program\, you will earn a Google Prompting 
 Essentials certificate to share on your resume\, LinkedIn and social media
  profiles!\nWhat You'll Learn\nThis program is designed for those with som
 e experience with using GenAI. Through short videos\, articles\, assignmen
 ts and quizzes\, you will discover:\nEssential\nPrompting Skills: How to u
 se a prompting framework to create a desired output with GenAI\; how to ev
 aluate and refine your results.\nEveryday Work Tasks:\nStrategies to draft
  content\, brainstorm ideas\, create tables\, timelines\, and more.\nData 
 & Presentations:\nHow to explore data visualization and use GenAI responsi
 bly when working with data.\nAdvanced Techniques:\nHow to use prompt chain
 ing for complex tasks and prompt versioning to save and reuse your best pr
 ompts over time.\nLearning Circles are study groups guided by\nlibrary sta
 ff for people who want to complete the Google Prompting Essentials special
 ization together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work toge
 ther through course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit to att
 ending all four learning circle sessions.\nSome Experience with GenAI Reco
 mmended: This course is ideal for participants who have completed the AI E
 ssentials course Learning Circle.\nHow to Joi\nn a Learning Circle:\nRegis
 ter once on the first session of this event series\, in order to attend al
 l sessions.\nPlease sign up with a\nvalid email address\n.\nAttend all fou
 r sessions at Keele Community Hub.\nRegistration is a two-step procedure. 
 First\, participants must complete their registration through this page. A
 fter this step\, library staff will follow up to request additional inform
 ation in order to complete the registration.\nInformation Collection Notic
 e:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publ
 ic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 2
 0(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration
 \, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your i
 nformation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 4
 16-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fb959c4134893003f0e7ce
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
