BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T200000
UID:697127ac4a9fd98b7f78e271@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the\ninformation session\non\nF
 riday\, April 24\, 2026.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Friday\,\nonce a we
 ek for 8 weeks\, May 1 - June 19\, 2026\, 5:00-8:00pm\n. Registration clo
 ses after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSn
 acks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists 
 will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\
 nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is sol
 ely responsible for the protection of \npersonal information collected thr
 ough the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, 2nd floor\, end of hallway
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/697127ac4a9fd98b7f78e271
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Between the Lines Bookclub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T200000
UID:6962837f91e4576f847bd100@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Become a page-turner by joining the Between the Lines Book Clu
 b! Here\, we embark on a new chapter with every read\, diving into a world
  of endless possibilities. From gripping thrillers to heartwarming coming-
 of-age tales\, or a sprinkle of fantasy adventures\, there's something for
  everyone. Whether you're a die-hard fan of one genre or love mixing thing
 s up\, you'll find a place here to discuss\, share\, and connect with fell
 ow readers. Ready to explore different worlds and discover your next favor
 ite book? Join us and let?s turn the page together!\nFriday May 15:\nA Man
  Called Ove by Fredrik Backman\nA Man Called Ove by Fredrik Backman is a 
 heartwarming tale about a curmudgeonly\, solitary man named Ove\, whose ri
 gid routines and no-nonsense attitude mask a deep sense of loss and loneli
 ness. When a young family moves in next door\, their unintentional involve
 ment in his life slowly begins to unravel his hardened exterior. Through a
  series of touching and often humorous events\, Ove’s journey from isola
 tion to connection reminds us of the power of community\, love\, and secon
 d chances. It's a story about how even the most seemingly unapproachable p
 eople can have a profound impact on the world around them.\nFriday June 19
 \n: The Alchemist\nby Paulo Coelho\nThe Alchemist by Paulo Coelho is a sim
 ple yet deeply philosophical novel about following your dreams. It tells t
 he story of Santiago\, a young shepherd who embarks on a journey from Spai
 n to the Egyptian desert in search of treasure. Along the way\, he encount
 ers mentors and challenges that teach him about listening to his heart\, r
 ecognizing opportunity\, and pursuing his “Personal Legend.” Blending 
 elements of fable\, spirituality\, and adventure\, the book explores theme
 s of destiny\, courage\, and the idea that the universe supports those who
  truly commit to their dreams.\nIf you need help getting a copy of the boo
 k or have any questions\, please contact us at sastaff@tpl.ca or 416-393-7
 653. Copies of the monthly titles are available at the circulation desk.
LOCATION:Sanderson\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6962837f91e4576f847bd100
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Sinye Tang
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T235959
UID:6a299f022ea730c17ab5e092@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, works by artist Sinye Tang are 
 on display at Don Mills Branch.\nSinye Tang (she/her) is a Chinese-Canadia
 n artist\, food enthusiast\, and amateur kayaker residing in Toronto. Her 
 artwork is informed by urban forays into nature and in search of deliciou
 s bites. She enjoys starting her watercolours in nature or on the water\, 
 and collaborates often with her husband\, Evan Manuella\, on line and was
 h.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Pu
 blic Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at loc
 ations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural
  interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed 
 during branch open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a299f022ea730c17ab5e092
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Sharon Alex
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T235959
UID:6a20399b748daf857d5ab32e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, the works of artist Sharon Alex
  are on display at Albion Branch\nSharon is an artist based in Toronto. S
 he paints in watercolours and loves photography. Her poetry explores her i
 nner most thoughts and hope she opens something within yourself as well\n
 "I'm inspired by animals and nature and poetry. My purpose is to tap into 
 the intimate and make you pause and explore what is important to you".\nTh
 is exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Li
 brary provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations 
 across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural intere
 sts of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during 
 Albion branch's open hours. Please check the\nAlbion branch\npage before y
 ou visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nPhoto credit: Sharon Alex\,\nThe Monar
 ch\, Photograph\, 8x10.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a20399b748daf857d5ab32e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
