BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Documentary Screening: Parade: Queer Acts of Love & Resistance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T164500
UID:69c801a78089f23c676529a9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Parade: Queer Acts of Love & Resistance\ncaptures pivotal mome
 nts that sparked Canada’s 2SLGBTQI+ movement\, honouring the activists a
 nd elders whose resistance led to the rights we have today.\nThrough rarel
 y seen archival footage and first-person accounts\, audiences are brought 
 to the frontlines of the struggle. From police raids to early drag shows\,
  community organizing to the House of Commons—the complex history of the
  country’s diverse communities is brought to life. Key milestones illust
 rate the power of taking it into the streets and underscore how easily the
  rights we’ve fought for can be revoked\, making the documentary essenti
 al viewing for all Canadians.\nUnflinching\, bold\, enraging\, hopeful\;\n
 Parade\nis a vital new chapter in the queer canon.\nThis screening is pres
 ented in collaboration with the National Film Board of Canada\, which is
  Canada’s only public producer and distributor of Canadian films and s
 eries.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Theatre (downstairs)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c801a78089f23c676529a9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
