BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto: A City of Belonging
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T190000
UID:6a283aca16554cd59fc78825@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What corner of this city has made you feel like you're part of
  something? A park bench\, a kitchen table\, a subway car\, a stage? In th
 is 60-minute facilitated experience\, you'll be paired with someone\, to s
 hare and craft a personal story of a time and place in Toronto where you f
 elt a sense of belonging. Together\, we'll mark these moments on a large p
 hysical map of the city and contribute short\, anonymous reflections to a 
 growing collective archive.\nPart storytelling exercise\, part civic exper
 iment\, this activity sets the stage for the evening's conversation betwee
 n Julia Hotz and Tara Henley.\nThis interactive pre-show is followed by\nJ
 ulia Hotz: The Connection Cure\n\, which starts at 7pm in the Appel Salon.
  You can register for that event\nHERE\n\, but please note if you wish to 
 attend the pre-event activity you need to register separately\non this pag
 e\n.\n***\nThis program continues the Library's programming series explori
 ng social connection\, including activities and conversations designed to 
 spark meaningful connections – bringing people together in engaging and 
 unexpected ways.\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT\n:\nLocation:\nNovella Room\, Toron
 to Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor\, inside the Bram and 
 Bluma Appel Salon\nTime:\nDoors open 5:30 PM\, Event starts 6:00 PM.\nTick
 ets:\nFree registration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these event
 s to make sure that most people have an opportunity to attend. Tickets are
  guaranteed until 5:45pm or until capacity is reached. Any remaining space
  will be opened up to the rush line beginning at 5:45pm.\nFilming Notifica
 tion: You may be photographed or filmed during this program.\nTPL is commi
 tted to accessibility. If you are Deaf or have a disability and would like
  to request accommodation for this event\, please contact accessibleservic
 es@tpl.ca or 416-393-7099 at least three weeks prior to the event.\n***\nI
 nformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation.\nRegistrants may be
  contacted to fill out a brief survey following the program\n. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Bram and Bluma Appel Salon - NOVELLA 
 room\, Toronto Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a283aca16554cd59fc78825
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Writers Collective of Canada (WCC): Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T200000
UID:6a0266aff56bd86e00af0e15@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nA Writers Collective of Canada (WCC) workshop is unlike any other
 . We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\, l
 isten deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into yo
 ur story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\, a
 nd respect.\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. Materials are 
 provided.\nDrop in\, no registration required\n.\nPlease arrive a few minu
 tes early.
LOCATION:City Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0266aff56bd86e00af0e15
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
