BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Julia Hotz: The Connection Cure
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T200000
UID:69cd822b8089f23c67660d6d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:How do we build communities that prescribe connection rather t
 han isolation?\nIn her groundbreaking book\nThe Connection Cure: The Presc
 riptive Power of Movement\, Nature\, Art\, Service\, and Belonging\,\njour
 nalist Julia Hotz reveals a revolutionary approach to health that's spread
 ing across over thirty countries. Instead of defaulting to pharmaceuticals
 \, doctors and healthcare workers are writing prescriptions for community 
 activities. The results are remarkable\, patients reporting dramatic impro
 vements not just in symptoms\, but in their sense of purpose\, connection\
 , and joy.\nWhat role can public institutions like libraries play in becom
 ing hubs of social health? How do we shift from treating symptoms of sickn
 ess to reconnecting people with sources of wellness? And what would it mea
 n if we redesigned our cities\, our healthcare systems\, and our daily rou
 tines around the radical idea that human connection is medicine?\nJoin one
  of the leading voices on social prescribing for a conversation about tran
 sforming how we think about health\, community\, and what it means to trul
 y care for one another.\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books available f
 or purchase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nJulia Hotz\nTara Henley\nRead 
 more:\nThe Connection Cure\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nBram and Blu
 ma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor\
 nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registrat
 ion required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that the
  greatest number of people have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guarante
 ed until 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. Seating first come\, first s
 erved\nBar:\nBeer/wine available for purchase (debit/credit only).\nAccess
 ibility:\nTPL is committed to accessibility. If you are Deaf or have a dis
 ability and would like to request accommodation for this event\, please co
 ntact accessibleservices@tpl.ca or 416-393-7099 at least three weeks prior
  to the event.\n***\nThis event is part of our signature\nSalon Series\n\,
  where we host local and international authors\, artists and thinkers in c
 onversation about their new books and big ideas.\n***\nInformation Collect
 ion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Tor
 onto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c
 )\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program reg
 istration\, delivery and evaluation. Registrants may be contacted to fill 
 out a brief survey following the program. Questions about how the library 
 handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline
 @tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Bram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto 
 Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cd822b8089f23c67660d6d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T200000
UID:69960daf4a9fd98b7f7ed8f2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on Mon
 day\, May 25 from 5-7 PM.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Monday\,\nonce a w
 eek for 8 weeks\, June 1 - July 20\, 2026\, 5-8pm\n. Registration closes 
 after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks
  and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will
  be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGer
 stein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is solely
  responsible for the protection of personal information collected through
  the program registration process.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69960daf4a9fd98b7f7ed8f2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Sharon Alex
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T235959
UID:6a20399b748daf857d5ab331@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, the works of artist Sharon Alex
  are on display at Albion Branch\nSharon is an artist based in Toronto. S
 he paints in watercolours and loves photography. Her poetry explores her i
 nner most thoughts and hope she opens something within yourself as well\n
 "I'm inspired by animals and nature and poetry. My purpose is to tap into 
 the intimate and make you pause and explore what is important to you".\nTh
 is exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Li
 brary provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations 
 across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural intere
 sts of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during 
 Albion branch's open hours. Please check the\nAlbion branch\npage before y
 ou visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nPhoto credit: Sharon Alex\,\nThe Monar
 ch\, Photograph\, 8x10.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a20399b748daf857d5ab331
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Sinye Tang
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T235959
UID:6a299f022ea730c17ab5e095@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, works by artist Sinye Tang are 
 on display at Don Mills Branch.\nSinye Tang (she/her) is a Chinese-Canadia
 n artist\, food enthusiast\, and amateur kayaker residing in Toronto. Her 
 artwork is informed by urban forays into nature and in search of deliciou
 s bites. She enjoys starting her watercolours in nature or on the water\, 
 and collaborates often with her husband\, Evan Manuella\, on line and was
 h.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Pu
 blic Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at loc
 ations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural
  interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed 
 during branch open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a299f022ea730c17ab5e095
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
