BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seniors Remember Yorkville: Documentaries and Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T200000
UID:6a0f4619f6bd012f00696526@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Get a glimpse of Yorkville from the early 20\nth\ncentury to t
 he 1950s through the memories and family stories of people who were there.
  Back Lane Studios presents Mapping Our Memories\, a project collecting pl
 ace-based stories from older people in video and written formats. You'll l
 earn about:\nGeorge Macey's grandfather\, who for decades managed an apart
 ment building on Bloor Street just east of Avenue Road. George's father wa
 s one of those kids who used to swim in the buff in the Don River. He late
 r ran a Yorkville gas station.\nVerna Van Sickle\, who opened a record sto
 re at the corner of Cumberland Avenue and Yonge Steet in the mid-1950s\, j
 ust as Yorkville was starting to attract artists and musicians. Verna had 
 many famous visitors drop by.\nSheila McIlraith\, whose father was a docto
 r and had his office in their home on Sherbourne Street. She used to vis
 it the Yorkville Library every week with her mother and brother.\nWe'll sc
 reen a curated selection of short documentaries\, learn about Mapping Our 
 Memories\, and meet some of the people behind the stories during a Q&A.\nN
 o registration required.
LOCATION:Yorkville\, Main floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0f4619f6bd012f00696526
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
