BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fashion for the Planet: Collaborative Mending & Upcycling
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T200000
UID:6a04a1c24134893003f193b4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:With the rise of fast fashion brands and social media fueled c
 onsumption habits\, the fashion industry ranks as the 3rd most environment
 ally damaging industry. Everyone participates in this in some way\, so it 
 is important that people are given the information and tools to consume cl
 othing responsibly. This 4 session program will work towards providing sus
 tainable fashion literacy to participants by teaching them the environment
 al impacts of the fashion industry\, tips for conscious consumption\, and 
 practical tools to extend the life cycle of their clothing through proper 
 care techniques\, mending and alteration skills\, and creative up-cycling 
 workshops.\nThis Session\n:\nCollaborative Mending & Upcycling\nParticipan
 ts will bring a piece of clothing that needs mending or upcycling & we wil
 l work on them by hand together\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
  789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a04a1c24134893003f193b4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
