DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T200000
UID:695c47296f926136000e7e2b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us each month for a lively discussion about a carefully c
 hosen book.\nEach month's selection will be available after the previous m
 onth's meeting.\nJanuary 29: Permanent Astonishment by Tomson HIghway\nFeb
 ruary 26: Nutshell by Ian McEwan\nMarch 26: A Spell of Good Things by Ay
 obami Adebayo\nApril 30: On the Ravine by Vincent Lam\nMay 28: Denison Ave
 nue by Christina Wong\nJune 25: Knife\, Meditations After an Attempted Mu
 rder by Salman Rushdie\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal infor
 mation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the P
 ublic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information 
 will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalua
 tion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dire
 cted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yong
 e Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Gerrard/Ashdale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/695c47296f926136000e7e2b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
