BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Create Your Own Nature Reserve – Right at Home!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T150000
UID:69cd25ba129f12743835ccdf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Imagine visiting your favourite park or conservation area – 
 where the sights\, sounds\, and magic of nature fill you with wonder\, pea
 ce and a sense of connection. Now imagine not having to fight traffic and 
 use polluting fuels to get there!\nIn this presentation\, learn how you ca
 n reimagine your current space to bring you that same refreshing and relax
 ing nature vibe at home. Explore the immense potential of natural spaces 
 at home that protect biodiversity and help to mitigate and adapt to climat
 e change through careful plant choices\, design\, and maintenance.\nPresen
 ted by\nDorte Windmuller\nof the\nDavid Suzuki Foundation's Butterfly Rang
 ers\n\, who are community leaders in teaching and inspiring people to prot
 ect bees\, butterflies\, and wildflowers.\nThis program is part of TPL's\n
 Our Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Publi
 c Library\, South Chapter.\n​\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
  789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Cliffcrest
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cd25ba129f12743835ccdf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
