SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Sinye Tang
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T235959
UID:6a299f022ea730c17ab5e099@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, works by artist Sinye Tang are 
 on display at Don Mills Branch.\nSinye Tang (she/her) is a Chinese-Canadia
 n artist\, food enthusiast\, and amateur kayaker residing in Toronto. Her 
 artwork is informed by urban forays into nature and in search of deliciou
 s bites. She enjoys starting her watercolours in nature or on the water\, 
 and collaborates often with her husband\, Evan Manuella\, on line and was
 h.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Pu
 blic Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at loc
 ations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural
  interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed 
 during branch open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a299f022ea730c17ab5e099
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Sharon Alex
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T235959
UID:6a20399b748daf857d5ab335@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, the works of artist Sharon Alex
  are on display at Albion Branch\nSharon is an artist based in Toronto. S
 he paints in watercolours and loves photography. Her poetry explores her i
 nner most thoughts and hope she opens something within yourself as well\n
 "I'm inspired by animals and nature and poetry. My purpose is to tap into 
 the intimate and make you pause and explore what is important to you".\nTh
 is exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Li
 brary provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations 
 across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural intere
 sts of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during 
 Albion branch's open hours. Please check the\nAlbion branch\npage before y
 ou visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nPhoto credit: Sharon Alex\,\nThe Monar
 ch\, Photograph\, 8x10.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a20399b748daf857d5ab335
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
