BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Dancing Lines by Nevena Niagolova
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T235959
UID:69b823748d5e2d093365965e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, the works of artist Nevena Niag
 olova are on display at the Yorkville Branch in an exhibit titled Dancing
  Lines.\nArtist biography:\nFor Bulgarian-Canadian artist and architect Ne
 vena Niagolova\, creativity has always been an inseparable part of life. H
 er journey\, from fine arts in Bulgaria to degrees from OCADU and U of T
 \, fuels a multidisciplinary practice rooted in play and wonder. Her work 
 is an invitation to play\, to imagine\, and to connect with one another.\
 nArtist statement:\nMy artwork strives to create a sense of wonder and pla
 y. Diversity and inclusivity are intrinsic\, as my work begins with only l
 ines\, brushstrokes\, and colours. There is no prescribed way one should
  feel or one should think\, and no pre-defined themes that one should abid
 e to. It offers the freedom to be curious and to explore. This freedom ca
 n spark conversations—people can share what they see\, what they imagine
 \, what moves them. Those little connections can make one’s day more pl
 easant and rich.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogr
 am. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibit the
 ir work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the di
 verse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit 
 can be viewed during\nYorkville\nbranch open hours.\nFree. All are welcome
 .\nImage credit: Artist: Nevena Niagolova\; Title of piece: Untrue But S
 till
LOCATION:Yorkville\, Main floor\, art exhibit space
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b823748d5e2d093365965e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
