BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Travels of Odysseus
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T190000
UID:6a2035d8748daf857d5ab2fb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In Homer's ​\nThe Odyssey\n\, Odysseus narrates his wanderin
 gs on the way home from Troy to Ithaca to his hosts the Phaeacians. The ta
 les are often full of wondrous material: exotic peoples\, monsters\, gods 
 and goddesses\, and dangerous natural phenomena. Once back home\, however\
 , Odysseus\, in disguise as a stranger\, tells false travel tales with rea
 l geography and the real peoples of the Mediterranean.\nIn this lecture Pr
 of. Jonathan Burgess will discuss the theme of travel in\nThe Odyssey\n\, 
 focusing on the paradox between the fantastical true travels of Odysseus a
 nd the realistic "lying tales" on Ithaca\, as well as the persistent urge 
 to identify the "real-world" locations of Odysseus' return through unlikel
 y theories and maps.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall (first floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2035d8748daf857d5ab2fb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding a Job with ACCES Employment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T193000
UID:69ebdb675c04bc0fc0636d6c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Job Search Strategies & Networking\nThis session explores effe
 ctive job search techniques\, including online applications\, hidden job m
 arkets\, and networking strategies. Participants will learn how to leverag
 e platforms like LinkedIn and build meaningful professional connections.\n
 Participants are encouraged (but not required) to bring a copy of their re
 sume (digital or printed) for feedback.\nDrop-In. Space is limited.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room\, Basement Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ebdb675c04bc0fc0636d6c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monthly Movie Screening: I Like Movies
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T200000
UID:69e17936fca21471b7ef70d9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This month's feature:\nI Like Movies\nEnjoy a night at the mov
 ies! Join us for a free movie on the big screen in our accessible theatre.
 \nDescription: Socially awkward 17-year-old cinephile\, Lawrence Kweller\
 , is self-absorbed and movie-obsessed. Fully convinced he can earn $90\,00
 0 to achieve his dream of attending film school at NYU\, he gets a part-ti
 me job at Sequels video store. There older store manager\, Alana\, takes h
 im under her wing. Meanwhile Lawrence sabotages every high school relation
 ship he has with his narcissistic film snobbery. Faced with the impending 
 reality of university life\, Lawrence must change his ways.\nThis film is 
 rated 14A. 99 minutes. Start time is 6:00 pm. Drop in. All are welcome!
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Theatre (lower level)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e17936fca21471b7ef70d9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google Prompting Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T203000
UID:6a10b7db43b41b3d006870c5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ready to develop the skills to use generative AI (GenAI) tools
  effectively and responsibly for work and daily life? Join our staff-facil
 itated learning circle to complete the self-paced Google Prompting Essenti
 als course. By completing this program\, you will earn a Google Prompting 
 Essentials certificate to share on your resume\, LinkedIn and social media
  profiles!\nWhat You'll Learn\nThis program is designed for those with som
 e experience with using GenAI. Through short videos\, articles\, assignmen
 ts and quizzes\, you will discover:\nEssential\nPrompting Skills\n: How to
  use a prompting framework to create a desired output with GenAI\; how to 
 evaluate and refine your results.\nEveryday Work Tasks:\nStrategies to dra
 ft content\, brainstorm ideas\, create tables\, timelines\, and more.\nDat
 a & Presentations:\nHow to explore data visualization and use GenAI respon
 sibly when working with data.\nAdvanced Techniques:\nHow to use prompt cha
 ining for complex tasks and prompt versioning to save and reuse your best 
 prompts over time.\nLearning Circles are study groups guided by\nlibrary s
 taff for people who want to complete the Google Prompting Essentials speci
 alization together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work to
 gether through course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit to a
 ttending all four learning circle sessions.\nSome Experience with GenAI Re
 commended: This course is ideal for participants who have completed the AI
  Essentials course Learning Circle.\nHow to Joi\nn a Learning Circle:\nReg
 ister once on the first session of this event series\, in order to attend 
 all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a\nvalid email address\n.\nA valid TPL 
 library card is required for online circles.\nAttend all four sessions (
 online via Zoom\, date: July 9\, 16\, 23\,30 )\nRegistration is a two-ste
 p procedure. First\, participants must complete their registration through
  this page. After this step\, library staff will follow up to request addi
 tional information in order to complete the registration.\nInformation Col
 lection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the
  Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 
 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program
  registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library h
 andles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline
 @tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a10b7db43b41b3d006870c5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
