BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Between the Lines Bookclub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T200000
UID:6962837f91e4576f847bd101@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Become a page-turner by joining the Between the Lines Book Clu
 b! Here\, we embark on a new chapter with every read\, diving into a world
  of endless possibilities. From gripping thrillers to heartwarming coming-
 of-age tales\, or a sprinkle of fantasy adventures\, there's something for
  everyone. Whether you're a die-hard fan of one genre or love mixing thing
 s up\, you'll find a place here to discuss\, share\, and connect with fell
 ow readers. Ready to explore different worlds and discover your next favor
 ite book? Join us and let?s turn the page together!\nFriday May 15:\nA Man
  Called Ove by Fredrik Backman\nA Man Called Ove by Fredrik Backman is a 
 heartwarming tale about a curmudgeonly\, solitary man named Ove\, whose ri
 gid routines and no-nonsense attitude mask a deep sense of loss and loneli
 ness. When a young family moves in next door\, their unintentional involve
 ment in his life slowly begins to unravel his hardened exterior. Through a
  series of touching and often humorous events\, Ove’s journey from isola
 tion to connection reminds us of the power of community\, love\, and secon
 d chances. It's a story about how even the most seemingly unapproachable p
 eople can have a profound impact on the world around them.\nFriday June 19
 \n: The Alchemist\nby Paulo Coelho\nThe Alchemist by Paulo Coelho is a sim
 ple yet deeply philosophical novel about following your dreams. It tells t
 he story of Santiago\, a young shepherd who embarks on a journey from Spai
 n to the Egyptian desert in search of treasure. Along the way\, he encount
 ers mentors and challenges that teach him about listening to his heart\, r
 ecognizing opportunity\, and pursuing his “Personal Legend.” Blending 
 elements of fable\, spirituality\, and adventure\, the book explores theme
 s of destiny\, courage\, and the idea that the universe supports those who
  truly commit to their dreams.\nIf you need help getting a copy of the boo
 k or have any questions\, please contact us at sastaff@tpl.ca or 416-393-7
 653. Copies of the monthly titles are available at the circulation desk.
LOCATION:Sanderson\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6962837f91e4576f847bd101
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
