BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Data Science Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T193000
UID:6a10653dc7d3cd58005ae1d7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about Data Science? Let's take a free o
 nline course together in a welcoming space!\nTogether we will work through
  Cisco Networking Academy's Introduction to Data Science course over six w
 eeks\, where we'll be introduced to basic concepts\, including:\nIntroduct
 ory analytics\nData collection\nData storage\nAI and machine learning\nPar
 ticipants will learn together in a peer-supported environment through a le
 arning circle\, a lightly facilitated study group guided by library staff.
 \nLearners who successfully complete the course will earn a digital badge 
 and certificate of completion.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe person
 al information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library und
 er the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The info
 rmation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery an
 d evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can
  be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 
 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Computer Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a10653dc7d3cd58005ae1d7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Managing Invasive Plants Around Your Home
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T200000
UID:69ac42dc8089f23c67606e33@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff for a presentation o
 n invasive plants commonly found around homes in Toronto. Learn how to ide
 ntify these species\, understand their impact\, and how to manage them. Yo
 u’ll also get tips on supporting local biodiversity through enhancing na
 tive habitats. Perfect for gardeners\, homeowners\, and anyone interested 
 in urban ecology.\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprog
 ram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapte
 r.​\nNo registration. Drop-in.
LOCATION:Yorkville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ac42dc8089f23c67606e33
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
