DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260831T200000
UID:69ecbe3bdefec6489cc01ea1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Award-winning crime writer Howard Shrier (\nMontreal Noir\n\;\
 nBuffalo Jump\n) shares techniques for building suspense in stories of cri
 me and mystery. With a short reading of a suspenseful passage from his new
  novel and by drawing on his experience as an author and creative writing 
 teacher\, Howard will show you how to create an outline that takes your ch
 aracters on the most challenging journey possible.\nInformation Collection
  Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toront
 o Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\,
  and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regist
 ration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles 
